## Backlog by Priority

### P0 (CRITICAL) - Production Blockers

#### P0-001: Fix Non-Functional Logs System
**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Large (4-6 hours)
**Dependencies**: None
**Spec Reference**: PROJECT.md (Logs Panel requirement) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-10-15-044325.md §"Critical Finding #1"

**Description**
The logs system is completely non-functional despite components existing. LogsPanel receives hardcoded empty array, LogsBar displays placeholder text "Log messages will appear here...", and the LogEntry type is not exported from types/index.ts. This violates CLAUDE.md's prohibition on fake demo data and prevents users from seeing application errors or status messages.

**Evidence from STATUS:**
- `src/components/App.tsx:72` - `<LazyLogsPanel logs={[]} />` (hardcoded empty array)
- `src/components/LogsBar.tsx:21` - Placeholder text instead of real data
- TypeScript errors: "Module has no exported member 'LogEntry'" in 2 files

**Acceptance Criteria**
- [ ] Export LogEntry type from `src/types/index.ts` with fields: timestamp, level, message, source
- [ ] Create logs state management in AppContext (useContext pattern)
- [ ] Implement logs collection from frontend events (errors, warnings, info)
- [ ] Add backend endpoint `/api/logs` to retrieve server-side logs (if doesn't exist)
- [ ] Connect LogsPanel to real log data from context (remove hardcoded empty array)
- [ ] Remove placeholder text from LogsBar and display actual recent log
- [ ] Test log display with real error scenarios (network errors, printer failures)
- [ ] Verify TypeScript compilation passes with LogEntry type fixes
- [ ] Integration test: Logs appear when errors occur in UI

**Technical Notes**
- LogEntry type likely exists somewhere but wasn't added to types/index.ts exports
- May need to create LogsContext provider wrapping App component
- Backend may already have logging infrastructure; check for existing log endpoints
- Follow pattern used by HistoryPanel for state management reference

---

#### P0-002: Fix TypeScript Strict Mode Violations
**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (2-3 hours)
**Dependencies**: P0-001 (LogEntry type export)
**Spec Reference**: CLAUDE.md (TypeScript strict mode requirement) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-10-15-044325.md §"Critical Finding #2"

**Description**
Despite `tsconfig.json` having `"strict": true"`, running `npm run typecheck` produces 18 compilation errors (6 fatal type errors + 12 unused variable warnings). The build succeeds because esbuild ignores TypeScript errors, creating illusory type safety. STATUS.md falsely claims "100% strict mode compliance."

**Evidence from STATUS:**
```
src/api/index.ts(4,3): error TS6133: 'PrintersResponse' is declared but never read
src/components/LazyHistoryPanel.tsx(111,6): error TS2375: Type incompatibility with exactOptionalPropertyTypes
src/components/LazyLogsPanel.tsx(2,10): error TS2305: Module has no exported member 'LogEntry'
src/components/LogsPanel.tsx(2,10): error TS2305: Module has no exported member 'LogEntry'
src/hooks/useLabels.ts(66,9): error TS2375: Type incompatibility with exactOptionalPropertyTypes
src/utils/error-tracking.ts(48,12): error TS2379: Argument type incompatibility
```
Plus 12 unused import warnings.

**Acceptance Criteria**
- [ ] Fix LogEntry type export errors (2 files) - covered by P0-001
- [ ] Fix exactOptionalPropertyTypes violations in LazyHistoryPanel.tsx (2 occurrences)
- [ ] Fix exactOptionalPropertyTypes violation in useLabels.ts
- [ ] Fix Sentry initialization type incompatibility in error-tracking.ts
- [ ] Remove all unused imports and variables (12 occurrences across 6 files)
- [ ] Run `npm run typecheck` - must pass with 0 errors
- [ ] Add `npm run typecheck` to CI/CD pipeline (package.json scripts or GitHub Actions)
- [ ] Update STATUS.md to remove false "100% strict mode compliance" claim
- [ ] Verify `npm run build` still succeeds after fixes

**Technical Notes**
- exactOptionalPropertyTypes errors occur when optional props have `| undefined` - remove the explicit undefined
- For Sentry type issues, may need to update @sentry/react version or adjust initialization options
- Use ESLint auto-fix for most unused variable removals: `npm run lint -- --fix`
- Files affected by unused imports: api/index.ts, HistoryPanel.tsx, PrinterPanel.tsx, useLocalStorage.ts, main.tsx, error-tracking.ts

**Files to Fix:**
1. `src/api/index.ts` - Remove unused PrintersResponse
2. `src/components/HistoryPanel.tsx` - Remove unused state, historyCount
3. `src/components/PrinterPanel.tsx` - Remove unused useState, togglePrinterPanel, connectionStatus
4. `src/components/LazyHistoryPanel.tsx` - Fix exactOptionalPropertyTypes (line 111)
5. `src/hooks/useLabels.ts` - Fix exactOptionalPropertyTypes (line 66)
6. `src/hooks/useLocalStorage.ts` - Remove unused useEffect
7. `src/main.tsx` - Remove unused React import
8. `src/utils/error-tracking.ts` - Remove unused getCurrentScope, fix Sentry init types

