#### P0-003: Fix Integration Test Failures
**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-4 hours)
**Dependencies**: None
**Spec Reference**: TESTING.md (integration tests) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-10-15-044325.md §"Test Failures"

**Description**
2 integration tests failing due to backend error response format not matching TypeScript type contracts. When backend returns errors, it sends `{ error: 'Server error' }` but TypeScript types expect `{ success: boolean, data: {...} }`. This creates runtime type validation failures and prevents proper error handling.

**Evidence from STATUS:**
```
Test Suite: tests/integration/printer-discovery-workflow.test.ts
Failure 1: Network timeout error handling - console.error shows error but test expects throw
Failure 2: Validation error for server error response
  Expected: { success: boolean, data: {...} }
  Received: { error: 'Server error' }
```

**Acceptance Criteria**
- [ ] Standardize Flask backend error response format across all endpoints
- [ ] Backend error format: `{ success: false, error: { code: string, message: string } }`
- [ ] Update DiscoveryResponse type to include error cases properly
- [ ] Update all API response types to handle error format consistently
- [ ] Fix network timeout handling in API client (should catch and transform errors)
- [ ] Verify all Flask endpoints return consistent format (check /printers, /preview, /print_labels, /discover)
- [ ] Update integration tests to match actual backend behavior
- [ ] Run full test suite: `pytest` must show 114/114 passing
- [ ] Document error response format in API documentation

**Technical Notes**
- Flask backend files to update: label_bro/app.py (all route handlers)
- TypeScript types to update: src/types/index.ts (all *Response types)
- Consider creating a standard error response wrapper in Flask
- May need to update API client error handling in src/api/index.ts

**Backend Endpoints to Audit:**
1. `/printers` - GET printer list
2. `/printers/discover` - POST full discovery
3. `/printers/test` - POST manual connection test
4. `/preview` - POST label preview
5. `/print_labels` - POST print job

